    "narrative": "The Austin Waves\u2019 lineup today is headlined by the aggressive efficiency of **Gunnar Henderson** (81.88) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.10), both of whom benefit from prime matchup conditions. **Gunnar Henderson** holds our highest score, propelled by a favorable 4.60 xERA matchup against Severino and a massive 16% park factor boost that maximizes his power-speed upside. Similarly, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** thrives against Alcantara with a 14% platoon edge and an 11% boost from the pitcher's profile, making him a cornerstone play. **Jackson Merrill** and **Kyle Tucker** provide strong secondary support, with **Jackson Merrill** specifically exploiting a 13% dynamic platoon advantage, while **Kyle Tucker** remains a high-floor staple despite a relatively neutral matchup against Elder.\n\nThe most difficult decision on the bench was **Nasim Nunez** (53.72), who narrowly missed the starting cut despite a favorable matchup against Alcantara. While **Nasim Nunez**\u2019s speed profile and the slow delivery of the opposing pitcher theoretically create an elite stolen base environment, his 9th-order slot dragged his efficiency score below that of our primary MI and corner infield options. Elsewhere, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (57.42) and **Brady House** (59.93) face the same Alcantara assignment; **Brady House** earns the slight nod over deeper bench options because his specific BvP and delivery-related boost offsets his lower raw base projection. \n\nStrategic risks for today center on the OF1 slot, where **Sam Antonacci** (46.73) faces a stiff test against Gilbert. While **Sam Antonacci** maintains an elite xwOBA, the 19% penalty assigned to his SP skill matchup makes this a marginal start; we are relying on his leadoff placement to drive value in the R and SB categories. Managers should monitor weather updates for all contests, as we are navigating a slate where nearly half the lineup faces hurlers with xERAs above 4.00, providing an ideal offensive setup for a team currently leaning heavily into stolen base opportunities. Note that **Luis Robert Jr.** remains sidelined, and we continue to monitor the utility spot held by **Josh Jung**, who provides stability but lacks the explosive upside needed to climb out of the mid-50s against Taillon.",
